lion in 2026, rising to $1.8 trillion in 2050. | source: Global AI Infrastructure Spending Will Hit $31.6 Trillion by 2050. This Is the Stock That Could Benefit the Most (fool.com) input gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca\n  - e5025 [third_party_view; 2026-09-19; push toward_last] NVIDIA forecasts that the five largest AI hyperscalers will spend nearly $800 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026. | source: Better Artificial Intelligence (AI) Stock Pick for 2027: Nvidia versus Micron (fool.com) input gnews:4ee5d8f73b7bcfc2f2111ad1\n- A random sample of uncited evidence in force (seed 20261120):\n  - e2007 [party_statement; 2026-08-17] Microsoft, Amazon, Alphabet, Meta and other hyperscalers guided combined 2026 capital spending of roughly $720 billion to $745 billion, about 77% above the prior year. | source: What Nvidia's $500 billion Wall Street deal signals about the AI boom (euronews.com) input gnews:29a55abcd8083e8aba1a8cbd\n  - e970 [fact; 2026-07-26] Alphabet announced a further increase to its 2026 capital-expenditure plans. | source: Prediction: Nvidia Stock Will Hit $800 Per Share by 2030 (fool.com) input gnews:fddb23b609fb42502a9aabce\n  - e567 [third_party_view; 2026-07-17] The author said investors feared lower-cost AI tokens would reduce or shift big tech's capital spending on AI infrastructure. | source: Why Did Nvidia Stock Sink Today? (fool.com) input gnews:bc598c1ba255001385a08723\n  - e1030 [third_party_view; 2026-07-27] Analysts expect Microsoft, Amazon and Meta to signal additional AI spending commitments in their results due this week; no amounts or periods are specified. | source: Apple stock surges past Nvidia to reclaim most valuable company title (qz.com) input gnews:b13ffbeffc140468830965b0\n  - e2368 [third_party_view; 2026-08-24] Dan Ives expected hyperscalers to continue raising capital and increasing capital expenditures; he gave no amount or period. | source: Dan Ives Has Message For Nvidia Stock Investors (tradingview.com) input gnews:5bdf65fa62553874d0da5a02\n\n## v6: How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\n\n- Looks at: Combined data-center capital expenditures by the four largest AI hyperscalers\n- Opened 2026-07-04 from: Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares? (fool.com); due 2028-03-31; open\n- Research groups: AI hyperscaler data-center capital spending\n- Answer ladder:\n  1. Below $800 billion: Combined spending is less than $800 billion.\n  2. $800 billion to below $900 billion: Combined spending is at least $800 billion and less than $900 billion.\n  3. $900 billion to below $1.1 trillion: Combined spending is at least $900 billion and less than $1.1 trillion.\n  4. $1.1 trillion to below $1.2 trillion: Combined spending is at least $1.1 trillion and less than $1.2 trillion.  <== current\n  5. $1.2 trillion or more: Combined spending is at least $1.2 trillion.\n- History: 43 judgements; first judged 2026-07-04 at rung 3; rung moves: 2026-08-26 3->4\n- Latest judgement 2026-09-19, why changed: The rung and central implied estimate are unchanged, but the new evidence includes a concrete Texas freeze on new grid connections, alongside specific utility hurdles. These add to the downside-risk facts; they do not quantify a spending reduction that would move the implied estimate across a rung boundary.\n- Latest reasoning: The market reference is approximately $1.08 trillion for calendar 2027, which is rung 3. The implied estimate remains about $1.19 trillion for the four named hyperscalers: apply the prior approximate four-to-five share proxy (about $730 billion of $800 billion) to NVIDIA’s $1.3 trillion top-five estimate. That is above rung 4’s $1.1 trillion floor but below rung 5’s $1.2 trillion floor. New grid-connection and other execution constraints increase downside risk, but the evidence does not quantify a reduction sufficient to cross either boundary; repeated reports of the $1.3 trillion estimate do not independently raise it. The share proxy is approximate because the underlying figures do not have perfectly matched scope.\n- Evidence in force: 87 (third_party_view 51, party_statement 33, fact 3)\n- Evidence cited by the latest judgement:\n  - e1926 [third_party_view; 2026-08-16; push none] Bank of America said analyst consensus for hyperscalers’ calendar 2027 spending rose from $480 billion in August 2025 to $1.08 trillion in August 2026, an increase of about 127%. | source: What Nvidia's $500 billion Wall Street deal signals about the AI boom (uk.finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:1219126db2e6631aa1264142\n  - e2535 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_last] NVIDIA said cloud-industry backlog exceeded $2 trillion and top-five hyperscaler capital expenditures were expected to approach $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027. | source: NVDA Q2 FY2027 Earnings Call (NVIDIA Corporation) input truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26\n  - e3391 [third_party_view; 2026-08-30; push toward_first] Ellen Hazen of F.L. Putnam said hyperscaler capital expenditures expected to exceed $1 trillion in calendar 2027 may not all be spent, citing labor, permitting, local-opposition and component constraints. | source: 'All about acceleration': After Nvidia earnings, the tech trade is getting more segmented (finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:9f03bbc66269c49a5ec8afee\n  - e3645 [fact; 2026-09-01; push toward_first] Texas has frozen new grid connections while officials audit developers. | source: Nvidia Slips as 700-Gigawatt Data-Center Pipeline Faces Texas Scrutiny (gurufocus.com) input gnews:b7a72f34e62112b669d71e36\n  - e3646 [third_party_view; 2026-09-01; push toward_first] Utilities in other markets are demanding upfront cash or proof that developers control proposed data-center sites. | source: Nvidia Slips as 700-Gigawatt Data-Center Pipeline Faces Texas Scrutiny (gurufocus.com) input gnews:b7a72f34e62112b669d71e36\n  - e4756 [party_statement; 2026-09-15; push toward_last] NVIDIA said the top five hyperscalers are expected to spend nearly $800 billion on capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027. | source: AI Extinction Fears Could Crush Nvidia’s $1.3 Trillion Growth Engine, but Don’t Panic Sell Just Yet (barchart.com) input gnews:5adb2372d28f9339f479435d\n  - e4789 [party_statement; 2026-09-16; push toward_last] NVIDIA management pegged the top five hyperscalers' CapEx at nearly $800 billion in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027. | source: Think Nvidia Is Overpriced? The Irony Keeps Me Buying Again and Again (finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:3f21db1f9791e20f80909da8\n  - e4857 [party_statement; 2026-09-16; push toward_last] NVIDIA estimates top-five hyperscaler capex could reach $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027, up from $800 billion in calendar 2026. | source: What Nvidia and SK Hynix Are Signaling About Micron's Outlook (fool.com) input gnews:4fbadb3b4cb5846297a34b0a\n  - e4990 [party_statement; 2026-09-18; push toward_last] NVIDIA projects the top five U.S. hyperscalers’ capital expenditure will reach $1.3 trillion in 2027. | source: Global AI Infrastructure Spending Will Hit $31.6 Trillion by 2050. This Is the Stock That Could Benefit the Most (fool.com) input gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca\n- A random sample of uncited evidence in force (seed 20261120):\n  - e4755 [party_statement; 2026-09-15] OpenAI CEO Sam Altman said OpenAI would use independent evaluators and agreed that frontier AI development needs to be paced. | source: AI Extinction Fears Could Crush Nvidia’s $1.3 Trillion Growth Engine, but Don’t Panic Sell Just Yet (barchart.com) input gnews:5adb2372d28f9339f479435d\n  - e3686 [third_party_view; 2026-09-01] The author argued that AI will require systemwide computer upgrades and exponentially more infrastructure to handle AI workloads. | source: Nvidia Just Slid 5% Post-Earnings. Again. CEO Jensen Huang Insists \"This Time Is Different.\" Is the Stock Still a Buy? (fool.com) input gnews:0295f27f6c1a83738ef035a9\n  - e3485 [party_statement; 2026-08-31] NVIDIA said capital expenditures by the five largest U.S. hyperscalers could rise from $800 billion in 2026 to $1.3 trillion in 2027. | source: Prediction: This Is Where Nvidia Stock Will Be When September Ends (fool.com) input gnews:a6dd88163443f40d35bdbdee\n  - e3124 [party_statement; 2026-08-28] NVIDIA expects industry hyperscale capital spending to approach $800 billion in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027. | source: Nvidia’s (NVDA) Earnings Shock Reignites Faith In The AI Boom (finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:c49ad54fc1f569a72b249821\n  - e3644 [third_party_view; 2026-09-01] The author said electricity requests across parts of the United States exceed 700 GW, more than ten times estimated current data-center consumption. | source: Nvidia Slips as 700-Gigawatt Data-Center Pipeline Faces Texas Scrutiny (gurufocus.com) input gnews:b7a72f34e62112b669d71e36\n\n## v9: How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n\n- Looks at: NVIDIA FY2027 Data Center segment revenue\n- Opened 2026-07-06 from: NVIDIA Falls 7% in a Month: Should You Still Hold NVDA Stock or Exit? (tradingview.com); due 2027-02-28; open\n- Research groups: none\n- Answer ladder:\n  1. Strongly bullish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $450 billion.\n  2. Bullish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $400 billion and below $450 billion.  <== current\n  3. Neutral: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion.\n  4. Bearish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\n  5. Strongly bearish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is below $300 billion.\n- History: 74 judgements; first judged 2026-07-06 at rung 2; rung moves: 2026-07-10 2->3, 2026-07-12 3->2, 2026-07-15 2->3, 2026-07-22 3->2, 2026-08-07 2->1, 2026-08-08 1->2, 2026-09-15 2->3, 2026-09-20 3->2\n- Latest judgement 2026-09-20, why changed: The rung moves from 3 to 2 because the quantified SemiAnalysis forecast for second-half revenue above analyst estimates lifts the implied FY2027 outcome across $400 billion, while the Q3 guide and first-half reported revenue anchor the estimate. The updated China-authorization theme adds some upside possibility, but NVIDIA's stated no-China-revenue outlook prevents treating that as booked revenue.\n- Latest reasoning: The market reference is approximately $414 billion for FY2027, which is rung 2. The evidence-based estimate is now around $410 billion: NVIDIA reported $164 billion in the first half, Q3 total-revenue guidance and the recent Data Center mix imply roughly $100 billion for Q3, and a roughly $146 billion Q4 is supported by the expected hyperscale reacceleration and Rubin ramp. SemiAnalysis's forecast of second-half Data Center revenue 20% above analyst estimates is a meaningful upside input: applying it to the roughly $250 billion of second-half revenue implied by the $414 billion reference would point to about $464 billion for the year. I discount that forecast because it does not state its underlying estimate and its implied Q4 is much higher than the company has quantified; the resulting central estimate remains near $410 billion. That crosses the $400 billion boundary into rung 2, but not the $450 billion boundary. Supply and competition risks, and NVIDIA's exclusion of China compute revenue from its outlook, temper the upside.\n- Evidence in force: 1287 (fact 614, party_statement 356, third_party_view 283, rumour 34)\n- Evidence cited by the latest judgement:\n  - e74 [fact; 2026-07-06; push toward_first] NVIDIA’s Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenue in FY2027 Q1, equal to 92% of total sales, up 92% year over year and 21% sequentially. | source: NVIDIA Falls 7% in a Month: Should You Still Hold NVDA Stock or Exit? (tradingview.com) input gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a\n  - e2517 [fact; 2026-08-26; push toward_first] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% year over year. | source: NVIDIA Corporation - NVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Second Quarter Fiscal 2027 (investor.nvidia.com) input extra:2799d8731e89b90c9bd3f108\n  - e2574 [fact; 2026-08-26; push toward_first] NVIDIA reported second-quarter FY2027 Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially, driven by the Blackwell Ultra ramp. | source: NVDA 8-K EX-99.2 (NVIDIA Corporation) input edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000073:q2fy27cfocommentary.htm\n  - e4995 [fact; 2026-09-18; push toward_first] NVIDIA generated $164 billion in Data Center segment revenue in the first six months of FY2027. | source: Global AI Infrastructure Spending Will Hit $31.6 Trillion by 2050. This Is the Stock That Could Benefit the Most (fool.com) input gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca\n  - e2848 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_first] NVIDIA guided to third-quarter revenue of $108 billion, with some revenue expected from Rubin GPUs. | source: Amazon just tripled its order of Nvidia chips over ‘surging demand’ (techcrunch.com) input gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a\n  - e3219 [third_party_view; 2026-08-28; push toward_first] Daniel Sparks calculated that FY2027 Q3 Data Center revenue would be $99.9 billion if its share of total revenue stayed at FY2027 Q2's 92.5%. | source: Prediction: Nvidia's Data Center Business Alone Clears $100 Billion in a Quarter This Fiscal Year (fool.com) input gnews:387b486b6e29491b9c8506df\n  - e2567 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_first] NVIDIA expected Vera Rubin to account for approximately 20% of Q3 FY2027 Data Center revenue. | source: NVDA Q2 FY2027 Earnings Call (NVIDIA Corporation) input truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26\n  - e3222 [party_statement; 2026-08-28; push toward_first] NVIDIA said hyperscale-business growth should reaccelerate in FY2027 Q4 as Vera Rubin supply builds. | source: Prediction: N