26-07-26 3->2, 2026-08-11 2->3, 2026-08-19 3->2\n- Latest judgement 2026-09-20, why changed: The rung is unchanged, but the current assessment incorporates the newly specified estimate of more than $100 billion of demand left unfulfilled next year as a supply-side counterweight. Its timing and revenue impact are not specific enough to reduce the FY2027 run-rate estimate.\n- Latest reasoning: The reference is about $411 billion for FY2027, which sits at rung 2; the cited Zacks growth estimate also implies about $405 billion using FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion. The operating run-rate implies about $419 billion: estimate Q3 at roughly $113.5 billion by applying the cited average 3.1% beat to the $110.16 billion high end of guidance, then carry the guided 12% sequential growth forward to Q4, about $127 billion, alongside reported Q1 and Q2 revenue. Supply constraints are a meaningful downside risk, but the cited estimate of more than $100 billion in unfulfilled demand is for “next year” and is not quantified as a reduction to FY2027 revenue. The implied outcome remains above $400 billion and below $450 billion, so it stays at rung 2.\n- Evidence in force: 1329 (fact 509, party_statement 395, third_party_view 373, rumour 52)\n- Evidence cited by the latest judgement:\n  - e5056 [third_party_view; 2026-09-19; push none] Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA to generate around $411 billion of revenue in FY2027. | source: We could see the world's first $10 trillion company arrive in less than two years (supercarblondie.com) input gnews:01edb4d1fa96705133b29207\n  - e4702 [third_party_view; 2026-09-14; push none] Zacks consensus estimates NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue growth of 87.4% year over year and EPS growth of 93.5%. | source: NVIDIA vs. Marvell: Which AI Infrastructure Stock Is the Better Buy? (zacks.com) input gnews:1d3bc1ba4c2df5e998884bdb\n  - e4377 [fact; 2026-09-10; push none] NVIDIA reported FY2026 revenue of approximately $215.9 billion, up 65.5% year over year. | source: Advanced Micro Devices vs. Nvidia: Which Semiconductor Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026? (fool.com) input gnews:be51df202b76715f3d9023f3\n  - e238 [fact; 2026-07-12; push toward_first] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year. | source: Forget GPUs. Nvidia’s Next AI Gold Mine Could Be Even Bigger. (barchart.com) input gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff\n  - e2497 [fact; 2026-08-26; push toward_first] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 revenue of $96.2 billion, up 18% quarter over quarter and 106% year over year. | source: NVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Second Quarter Fiscal 2027 | NVIDIA Newsroom (NVIDIA Corporation) input nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027\n  - e2499 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_first] NVIDIA guided Q3 FY2027 revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, assuming no Data Center compute revenue from China. | source: NVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Second Quarter Fiscal 2027 | NVIDIA Newsroom (NVIDIA Corporation) input nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027\n  - e3943 [party_statement; 2026-09-04; push toward_first] NVIDIA's FY2027 Q3 guidance implied total revenue growth of 12% sequentially at the midpoint. | source: Jensen Huang's Nvidia Guided for 70% Revenue Growth in Fiscal 2028, Far Above the 44% Wall Street Expected, as Amazon Agreed to Buy 2 Million Nvidia GPUs. Is the Growth Forecast Believable? (fool.com) input gnews:89698c9955cf8aa35b642970\n  - e4761 [third_party_view; 2026-09-15; push toward_first] Manali Pradhan forecast NVIDIA fiscal Q3 2027 revenue of around $113 billion to $114 billion. | source: Prediction: Nvidia's $108 Billion Q3 Guide Will Look Conservative by December (fool.com) input gnews:9fd93b942948c5002e13eb0b\n  - e4762 [third_party_view; 2026-09-15; push toward_first] Manali Pradhan said NVIDIA exceeded the high end of revenue guidance in each of the past 12 quarters, averaging 3