ross-margin guidance, which sits at rung 3. The reported 75% margins in Q1 and Q2, followed by guidance of 74% in Q3 and 71%–72% in Q4, imply roughly 73.6%–73.7% for FY2027 when carried through the year with the guided revenue growth. That is below the reference midpoint but remains above the 73% rung boundary. Memory-cost pressure and potentially dilutive H200 sales weigh on the estimate; the indicated pricing recovery begins in FY2028, while potentially favorable HBM pricing is an offset. None of the sized or quantified evidence shifts the FY2027 estimate below 73%.\n- Evidence in force: 222 (party_statement 100, third_party_view 57, fact 54, rumour 11)\n- Evidence cited by the latest judgement:\n  - e1474 [party_statement; 2026-08-06; push none] NVIDIA guided fiscal 2027 gross margin to the mid-seventies. | source: What You Are Actually Underwriting In NVIDIA Stock (trefis.com) input gnews:005ecb2260c71807a6d9b7c1\n  - e1794 [fact; 2026-08-13; push toward_first] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q1 non-GAAP gross margin of 75.0%. | source: I’m Buying More and More Nvidia Because Of One Massive AI Transition Underway (247wallst.com) input gnews:1258c8b56ae0bb231116e1e5\n  - e2498 [fact; 2026-08-26; push toward_first] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins of 75.0%. | source: NVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Second Quarter Fiscal 2027 | NVIDIA Newsroom (NVIDIA Corporation) input nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027\n  - e2569 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_last] NVIDIA guided Q3 FY2027 GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins to 74% ±0.5 percentage points, Q4 FY2027 margins to 71–72%, and FY2028 margins to 72–73%. | source: NVDA Q2 FY2027 Earnings Call (NVIDIA Corporation) input truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26\n  - e2570 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_last] NVIDIA said memory prices had risen more than previously expected and were expected to increase further in FY2028. | source: NVDA Q2 FY2027 Earnings Call (NVIDIA Corporation) input truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26\n  - e2625 [fact; 2026-08-26; push toward_last] NVIDIA recorded a $0.4 billion H200-related excess inventory and purchase-obligation charge in FY2027 first half as H200 demand diminished. | source: NVDA 10-Q 10-Q (NVIDIA Corporation) input edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000075:nvda-20260726.htm\n  - e2627 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_last] NVIDIA said H200s shipped under the U.S. licensing program incur a 25% U.S. import tariff, none of which it has passed on to customers or expects to pass on if China sales resume. | source: NVDA 10-Q 10-Q (NVIDIA Corporation) input edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000075:nvda-20260726.htm\n  - e2674 [third_party_view; 2026-08-26; push toward_last] Jim Cramer cited an estimated 2% gross-margin impact from higher DRAM costs. | source: Jim Cramer Says Nvidia Is 'Not Going to Stop Here' as Ross Gerber Sees NVDA Stock Hitting $450 as Analysts Dissect Q2 Earnings (benzinga.com) input gnews:1c1eb52d79237b26874d76c7\n  - e3153 [party_statement; 2026-08-28; push toward_last] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said negotiated price increases would take effect in Q1 FY2028 and support gross-margin recovery. | source: Nvidia's Margin Pressure Is Micron's Revenue Boost (fool.com) input gnews:92e19c04dbca319f84450451\n  - e3154 [party_statement; 2026-08-28; push toward_last] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said Hopper 200 sales to China under U.S. licenses were less than 1% of Data Center revenue and diluted corporate gross margin. | source: Nvidia's Margin Pressure Is Micron's Revenue Boost (fool.com) input gnews:92e19c04dbca319f84450451\n  - e3189 [party_statement; 2026-08-28; push toward_last] NVIDIA guided FY2027 third-quarter revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, and gross margin to 74%, plus or minus 50 basis points. | source: Jim Cramer Says Own NVIDIA (NVDA) After Another Blowout Quarter (finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:95b31c79c355868ea4f25633\n  - e3746 [third_party_view; 2026-09-01; push toward_first] The author believes NVIDIA has likely secured a long-term SOCAMM agreement with SK Hynix, favorable HBM pricing, and large HBM volume commitments for 2027, while noting the final negotiation could differ from the estimate. | source: Korea’s Trillion-Dollar Sovereign AI Investment: Nvidia Wins, Hynix Loses (newsletter.semianalysis.com) input gnews:d30249a09f7f187ba29fbbde\n  - e3807 [third_party_view; 2026-09-03; push toward_last] SK Hynix predicted that the DRAM market would remain supply-constrained through at least 2030. | source: Nvidia vs. Micron: Which Is the Better AI Semiconductor Stock to Own for the Next 5 Years? (fool.com) input gnews:bdeea3eb75a259e6ec118c55\n  - e4456 [rumour; 2026-09-11; push toward_last] Reports of a possible TSMC price increase of up to 10% in 2027 raise the prospect of higher manufacturing costs for NVIDIA. | source: TSM’s Record Sales Say AI Chips Are Booming. The Nvidia-AMD Fight Is Now About Who Keeps the Margin (finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:c5641df9bbd4bd4c27bfa16a\n  - e4855 [third_party_view; 2026-09-16; push toward_last] SK Hynix expects the memory shortage to worsen next year and estimates memory demand could exceed supply beyond 2030 despite adding capacity. | source: What Nvidia and SK Hynix Are Signaling About Micron's Outlook (fool.com) input gnews:4fbadb3b4cb5846297a34b0a\n  - e4905 [party_statement; 2026-09-18; push toward_first] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron were working with NVIDIA to increase memory capacity required by its roadmap. | source: Analysis: What Nvidia’s Massive Supply-Demand Gap Says About AI Mania (crn.com) input gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33\n- A random sample of uncited evidence in force (seed 20261120):\n  - e2664 [third_party_view; 2026-08-26] The article estimated that the reported 15% server price increase could add hundreds of thousands of dollars per rack for systems selling for millions of dollars each. | source: Nvidia’s AI Servers Are About to Get Pricier — What a 15%+ Hike Means for the Whole Stack (finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:c795bb21915f49451c0291c1\n  - e2516 [fact; 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins of 75.0%. | source: NVIDIA Corporation - NVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Second Quarter Fiscal 2027 (investor.nvidia.com) input extra:2799d8731e89b90c9bd3f108\n  - e3740 [third_party_view; 2026-09-01] The author says AI-infrastructure demand is driving memory shortages and higher memory prices, hurting NVIDIA and its peers. | source: Nvidia Shareholders Should Brace Themselves for 1 Particular Thing in the Months to Come. Here’s What It Means for the Long-term Picture. (fool.com) input gnews:ee0002bd6bda4aa8d9a483f5\n  - e1698 [third_party_view; 2026-08-11] The author characterized NVIDIA's gross margin as 71.07%. | source: I’m Buying Nvidia Ahead of Aug. 26 Earnings Exactly For The Reason You Think (247wallst.com) input gnews:85df0dfbd885d4e92e530768\n  - e3333 [party_statement; 2026-08-29] NVIDIA guided to FY2027 third-quarter GAAP and non-GAAP gross margin of 74%, plus or minus 50 basis points. | source: Nvidia's CFO Just Explained Why the AI Boom Is Eating Its Gross Margin -- and It's a Green Light for Micron (fool.com) input gnews:69d682468e018e0065df5180\n\n## v34: Will NVIDIA sign an agreement to acquire Hugging Face by 2027-02-26?\n\n- Looks at: Whether NVIDIA signs an agreement to acquire Hugging Face\n- Opened 2026-08-26 from: Nvidia closes in on Hugging Face acquisition (techcrunch.com); due 2027-02-26; open\n- Research groups: NVIDIA–Hugging Face acquisition talks\n- Answer ladder:\n  1. Yes: NVIDIA signs an agreement to acquire Hugging Face on or before 2027-02-26.  <== current\n  2. No: NVIDIA has not signed an agreement to acquire Hugging Face by 2027-02-26.\n- History: 26 judgements; first judged 2026-08-26 at rung 1; rung moves: none\n- Latest judgement 2026-09-20, why changed: The rung and the key supporting fact are unchanged: the definitive agreement was signed on September 2, 2026. Later reports largely repeat that fact or address the transaction's terms, rationale, or expected closing rather than changing the signing outcome.\n- Latest reasoning: The reference is rung 2 (No): no separate market consensus or signing deadline is supplied, so the status quo is no signed agreement. The definitive-agreement filing says NVIDIA entered into the agreement on September 2, 2026, before the February 26, 2027 deadline, so the implied outcome is rung 1. Later reports about regulatory review or closing do not change whether the agreement was signed.\n- Evidence in force: 180 (fact 68, party_statement 39, third_party_view 37, rumour 36)\n- Evidence cited by the latest judgement:\n  - e3768 [fact; 2026-09-03; push toward_first] NVIDIA signed a definitive agreement on September 2, 2026 to acquire Hugging Face for approximately $11.9 billion, with up to approximately $1.0 billion in employee retention awards, and expects the deal to close in the first half of 2027 subject to conditions including regulatory approvals. | source: NVDA 8-K 8-K (NVIDIA Corporation) input edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000078:nvda-20260902.htm\n  - e5086 [fact; 2026-09-20; push toward_first] NVIDIA signed a definitive agreement to acquire Hugging Face on September 2, 2026; Jensen Huang disclosed the deal on September 3. | source: NVIDIA to Acquire Hugging Face for Approximately $12.7 Billion in Strategic Pivot After Earlier Investment Rejection (finance.biggo.com) input gnews:7a5002df93385ecef12a2cd8\n- A random sample of uncited evidence in force (seed 20261120):\n  - e3358 [rumour; 2026-08-29] An unnamed source told CNBC that NVIDIA's acquisition of Hugging Face had been part of ongoing and recent talks. | source: Kevin Durant Is About To Make More Money From Nvidia Than His NBA Salary (sports.yahoo.com) input gnews:58e05f34f62fa84c762c5e85\n  - e3132 [rumour; 2026-08-28] Reuters reported on August 27 that NVIDIA had agreed to acquire Hugging Face. | source: Nvidia May Be Paying 86 Times Sales for Hugging Face And It Might Actually Make Sense: Here’s Why (finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:fd58858283c5243da428b65e\n  - e4273 [third_party_view; 2026-09-09] The author stated that NVIDIA was acquiring Hugging Face for $12.9 billion. | source: Here's My Nvidia Stock Price Forecast for the End of September (fool.com) input gnews:33edf25ec336133783ceead0\n  - e3821 [rumour; 2026-09-03] NVIDIA is reportedly in advanced talks to acquire Hugging Face for up to US$14 billion. | source: Nvidia (NVDA) Nears $14 Billion AI Deal As Copyright Case Heads To Court (finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:80ec71d0b21c1a76ec467cbb\n  - e3944 [fact; 2026-09-04] NVIDIA announced its intention to acquire Hugging Face for $12.9303 billion, including $11.9 billion for investors and up to $1 billion in equity-based retention for employees joining NVIDIA. | source: Nvidia plans to buy Hugging Face for an eye-watering $13 billion (finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:3d2ec04b23108e1ab4b18855\n\n## v43: Will the required U.S. and EU regulatory reviews of NVIDIA's Hugging Face acquisition be cleared by 2027-06-30?\n\n- Looks at: U.S. and EU regulatory review of NVIDIA's proposed Hugging Face acquisition\n- Opened 2026-09-20 from: NVIDIA to Acquire Hugging Face for Approximately $12.7 Billion in Strategic Pivot After Earlier Investment Rejection (finance.biggo.com); due 2027-06-30; open\n- Research groups: NVIDIA–Hugging Face acquisition talks\n- Answer ladder:\n  1. Yes: Required U.S. and EU regulatory clearances for the acquisition have been granted by 2027-06-30.  <== current\n  2. No: One or more required U.S. or EU regulatory clearances have not been granted by 2027-06-30.\n- History: 1 judgements; first judged 2026-09-20 at rung 1; rung moves: none\n- Latest judgement 2026-09-20, why changed: This is the first judgement.\n- Latest reasoning: The stated completion plan falls within the deadline and therefore implies clearance by 2027-06-30. The mandatory U.S. filing and The Register's call for intervention add some risk, but neither supplies a regulator's objection, a delay, or a specific reason the reviews will remain uncleared by the deadline, so the forecast does not cross to rung 2.\n- Evidence in force: 5 (fact 4, third_party_view 1)\n- Evidence cited by the latest judgement:\n  - e5086 [fact; 2026-09-20; push none] NVIDIA signed a definitive agreement to acquire Hugging Face on September 2, 2026; Jensen Huang disclosed the deal on September 3. | source: NVIDIA to Acquire Hugging Face for Approximately $12.7 Billion in Strategic Pivot After Earlier Investment Rejection (finance.biggo.com) input gnews:7a5002df93385ecef12a2cd8\n  - e5087 [fact; 2026-09-20; push none] NVIDIA agreed to acquire Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion. | source: NVIDIA to Acquire Hugging Face for Approximately $12.7 Billion in Strategic Pivot After Earlier Investment Rejection (finance.biggo.com) input gnews:7a5002df93385ecef12a2cd8\n  - e5088 [fact; 2026-09-20; push toward_first] NVIDIA and Hugging Face are targeting completion in the first half of 2027, subject to regulatory approvals including in the EU. | source: NVIDIA to Acquire Hugging Face for Approximately $12.7 Billion in Strategic Pivot After Earlier Investment Rejection (finance.biggo.com) input gnews:7a5002df93385ecef12a2cd8\n  - e5089 [fact; 2026-09-20; push toward_last] The Hugging Face acquisition meets the U.S. Hart-Scott-Rodino mandatory filing threshold, requiring notice to the FTC and DOJ. | source: NVIDIA to Acquire Hugging Face for Approximately $12.7 Billion in Strategic Pivot After Earlier Investment Rejection (finance.biggo.com) input gnews:7a5002df93385ecef12a2cd8\n  - e5090 [third_party_view; 2026-09-20; push toward_last] The Register argued that regulators should intervene in NVIDIA's proposed Hugging Face acquisition. | source: NVIDIA to Acquire Hugging Face for Approximately $12.7 Billion in Strategic Pivot After Earlier Investment Rejection (finance.biggo.com) input gnews:7a5002df93385ecef12a2cd8\n- A random sample of uncited evidence in force (seed 20261120):\n\n## Research groups\n- g1 NVIDIA AI-cloud revenue-sharing and credit-support model: v1, v2, v22\n- g2 NVIDIA AI Compute Partnership: v2, v3, v11, v22, v30, v31\n- g3 Vera Rubin rollout: v4, v37\n- g4 AI hyperscaler data-center capital spending: v5, v6\n- g5 Vera Rubin Ultra / Kyber rollout: v7\n- g6 China authorization of Nvidia H200 purchases: v10\n- g7 Firmus preference-share raising: v11\n- g8 GeForce RTX 60 rollout: v12\n- g9 French antitrust investigation into NVIDIA: v13\n- g10 NVIDIA Vera CPU rollout: v18\n- g11 Remote Access Security Act legislative process: v19\n- g12 NAVER GAK Sejong AI factory expansion and financing: v20\n- g13 NVIDIA investment and strategic partnership with Safe Superintelligence: v23, v29, v40\n- g14 RTX Spark rollout: v24\n- g15 Taiwan advanced-chip export-control consultations: v25\n- g16 Taiwan AI chip export restrictions: v26\n- g17 U.S. investigation into Chinese access to advanced chips: v27\n- g18 NVIDIA investment in SB Energy: v31\n- g19 NVIDIA-Poolside AI technology license and investment: v32\n- g20 NVIDIA–Hugging Face acquisition talks: v34, v43\n- g21 NVIDIA investment and expanded partnership with MediaTek: v36\n- g22 Rubin CPX rollout: v37\n- g23 Thinking Machines Lab funding round: v38\n- g24 U.S. Justice Department review of NVIDIA’s Groq transaction: v39\n- g25 Federal Reserve September 2026 policy meeting: v41\n- g26 AI Energy Management Alliance power-flexible data center: v42\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
