{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '198,222p;390,419p;530,551p' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-q/library-pack.md\"","aggregated_output":"  5. $800 billion or more: Combined spending is at least $800 billion.\n- History: 56 judgements; first judged 2026-07-04 at rung 3; rung moves: 2026-07-15 3->4, 2026-07-17 4->3, 2026-07-27 3->4, 2026-07-30 4->3, 2026-08-11 3->4\n- Latest judgement 2026-09-19, why changed: The rung and the key four-company estimate remain as in the previous conclusion. The newer nearly-$800-billion figures concern the top five or a broader AI data-center spending measure, and do not provide a new four-company figure; repeated claims do not independently change the forecast.\n- Latest reasoning: The market reference is roughly $720–$745 billion for the four companies, which is rung 4. A direct four-hyperscaler estimate of $760 billion and tracking near $745 billion support an implied outcome around $750–$760 billion. Newer estimates of nearly $800 billion refer to the top five, not these four, so the fifth company cannot be counted in full; the four-company outcome remains below the $800 billion rung-5 boundary. The revised company guidance and Microsoft's reported capex growth support a high total, while the cancellation, grid-connection and sustainability concerns are not quantified as changes to the four-company 2026 total.\n- Evidence in force: 160 (third_party_view 92, party_statement 45, fact 23)\n- Evidence cited by the latest judgement:\n  - e779 [fact; 2026-07-22; push toward_last] Microsoft capital expenditures were $30.88 billion in Q3 FY2026, up 84% year over year. | source: The Ultimate Bull Run for NVIDIA, Micron, and SanDisk May Be Closer Than Investors Think (247wallst.com) input gnews:ba97f512051bcb3ff34f5b05\n  - e1091 [party_statement; 2026-07-27; push toward_last] Alphabet raised its 2026 capital expenditure guidance to $195 billion–$205 billion, from $180 billion–$190 billion previously. | source: Alphabet's Massive AI Investment Push Signals More Gains Ahead for Nvidia (fool.com) input gnews:ac966c48ae5afea2a79acaf3\n  - e1094 [party_statement; 2026-07-27; push toward_last] Alphabet CEO Sundar Pichai said demand for Alphabet's AI models was outpacing supply and that management was ramping up capital spending to convert backlog into revenue. | source: Alphabet's Massive AI Investment Push Signals More Gains Ahead for Nvidia (fool.com) input gnews:ac966c48ae5afea2a79acaf3\n  - e1373 [party_statement; 2026-08-01; push toward_last] Meta raised its FY26 capital expenditure guidance to $125 billion–$145 billion. | source: 5 Tech Stocks Most at Risk From NVIDIA’s Stranglehold on the Industry (247wallst.com) input gnews:c5ba7d4f41d0388a171eebcc\n  - e1490 [party_statement; 2026-08-06; push toward_last] Amazon raised its projected capital expenditures for calendar 2026 from $200 billion to $220 billion, with the increase mostly attributed to higher memory chip costs. | source: History Says This Is What Will Happen to Nvidia Stock After Aug. 26 (fool.com) input gnews:275ccde6edc6d12657c32c3e\n  - e1703 [third_party_view; 2026-08-11; push toward_last] Combined 2026 capital spending by the four largest hyperscalers was tracking near $745 billion. | source: NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang Just Announced $500 Billion in New Funding: Here's Why Amazon, Microsoft, and Google Are Taking It Hard. (247wallst.com) input gnews:61ba718265df905f5dcc9dad\n  - e1925 [third_party_view; 2026-08-16; push toward_last] Microsoft, Amazon, Alphabet, Meta and other hyperscalers have guided to roughly $720 billion–$745 billion of capital spending in calendar 2026, about 77% above the prior year. | source: What Nvidia's $500 billion Wall Street deal signals about the AI boom (uk.finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:1219126db2e6631aa1264142\n  - e2269 [third_party_view; 2026-08-23; push toward_last] The four largest hyperscalers plan a combined $760 billion of capital expenditures in calendar 2026. | source: I've Covered Nvidia for 9 Years. Here's Whether the Stock Is Overvalued Right Now. (fool.com) input gnews:c8ea23246edff9fbbc981992\n  - e3347 [third_party_view; 2026-08-29; push toward_first] TechRadar reported that $130 billion of AI data-center projects were cancelled or delayed in Q1 2026 because of public opposition. | source: Nvidia looks to set up an employee-funded political action committee to try and shape US policy in its favor (techradar.com) input gnews:295caa6e12f0b739d2e14ea6\n  - e3645 [fact; 2026-09-01; push toward_first] Texas has frozen new grid connections while officials audit developers. | source: Nvidia Slips as 700-Gigawatt Data-Center Pipeline Faces Texas Scrutiny (gurufocus.com) input gnews:b7a72f34e62112b669d71e36\n  - e3646 [third_party_view; 2026-09-01; push toward_first] Utilities in other markets are demanding upfront cash or proof that developers control proposed data-center sites. | source: Nvidia Slips as 700-Gigawatt Data-Center Pipeline Faces Texas Scrutiny (gurufocus.com) input gnews:b7a72f34e62112b669d71e36\n  - e4457 [third_party_view; 2026-09-11; push toward_last] NVIDIA estimates that the five largest AI hyperscalers will spend nearly $800 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026. | source: Apple, Microsoft, and Nvidia Top the List of Largest Companies by Market Cap. Here's the One I'm Buying Now. (fool.com) input gnews:3f69a17dc0ba27583e1dbd92\n  - e4497 [party_statement; 2026-09-11; push toward_first] On September 10, 2026, BIS General Manager Pablo Hernández de Cos said AI investment is increasingly financed with debt and private credit, and warned disappointing returns could trigger an investment pullback. | source: Nvidia's Huang Dismisses Circular Financing Worries, Touts $100 Billion Contract Backlog (finance.biggo.com) input gnews:8e160db6032cc34164f45e59\n  - e4696 [third_party_view; 2026-09-14; push toward_last] Amazon, Alphabet, Microsoft and Meta Platforms are expected to spend a combined $720 billion to $745 billion on capital expenditures in calendar 2026, with a large portion directed toward AI infrastructure. | source: NVIDIA vs. Marvell: Which AI Infrastructure Stock Is the Better Buy? (zacks.com) input gnews:1d3bc1ba4c2df5e998884bdb\n  - e4738 [third_party_view; 2026-09-15; push toward_last] BofA Global Research estimated that Microsoft, Alphabet, Amazon, Meta and Oracle could spend about $795 billion collectively on capital expenditures in calendar 2026. | source: Nvidia Rebounds, but AI's $1.08 Trillion Boom Faces Its First Brake (gurufocus.com) input gnews:ca2f580191a4509ac38bc1cf\n  - e4756 [party_statement; 2026-09-15; push toward_last] NVIDIA said the top five hyperscalers are expected to spend nearly $800 billion on capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027. | source: AI Extinction Fears Could Crush Nvidia’s $1.3 Trillion Growth Engine, but Don’t Panic Sell Just Yet (barchart.com) input gnews:5adb2372d28f9339f479435d\n  - e4994 [third_party_view; 2026-09-18; push toward_last] PwC projected annual AI data-center infrastructure spending of about $800 billion in 2026, rising to $1.8 trillion in 2050. | source: Global AI Infrastructure Spending Will Hit $31.6 Trillion by 2050. This Is the Stock That Could Benefit the Most (fool.com) input gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca\n  - e5025 [third_party_view; 2026-09-19; push toward_last] NVIDIA forecasts that the five largest AI hyperscalers will spend nearly $800 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026. | source: Better Artificial Intelligence (AI) Stock Pick for 2027: Nvidia versus Micron (fool.com) input gnews:4ee5d8f73b7bcfc2f2111ad1\n- A random sample of uncited evidence in force (seed 20261120):\n  - e338 [fact; 2026-07-14; push toward_last] Beijing refused to authorize Chinese companies to buy Nvidia H200 GPUs and relied on domestic semiconductor manufacturers to address the shortfall. | source: Nvidia slashes list of authorized customers in Asia in a bid to reduce AI chip smuggling, report claims — company sent field inspectors, called customers to check if business is genuine after pressure from Washington (tomshardware.com) input gnews:2a41a34c16f5280b624481fb\n  - e354 [rumour; 2026-07-14; push toward_first] Unnamed sources said some Chinese cloud firms recently told partners and clients they may soon be able to obtain H200 chips, suggesting progress in Chinese import reviews. | source: Exclusive-ZTE among Chinese firms licensed to purchase Nvidia's H200 chips, documents show (ca.finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:24268bfaab6ef1d7876b188c\n  - e2160 [rumour; 2026-08-19; push toward_first] ByteDance and Tencent each reportedly took delivery of roughly 10,000 NVIDIA H200 accelerators in recent weeks, the first meaningful shipments into mainland China since export approval. | source: First Nvidia H200 shipments reach China, ByteDance and Tencent take deliveries as Beijing loosens its import block — most licensed chips must stay in Hong Kong, which can't power them (tomshardware.com) input gnews:38ac6220787b05226cf31f1f\n  - e2161 [rumour; 2026-08-19; push toward_last] Beijing is directing Chinese buyers to keep most of their U.S.-licensed H200 allowance, up to 100,000 chips per company, in Hong Kong rather than mainland China. | source: First Nvidia H200 shipments reach China, ByteDance and Tencent take deliveries as Beijing loosens its import block — most licensed chips must stay in Hong Kong, which can't power them (tomshardware.com) input gnews:38ac6220787b05226cf31f1f\n  - e2163 [rumour; 2026-08-19; push toward_first] Lenovo and other NVIDIA partners told Chinese customers last week they could resume orders for H200-based AI servers, subject to separate NDRC approval for each purchase. | source: First Nvidia H200 shipments reach China, ByteDance and Tencent take deliveries as Beijing loosens its import block — most licensed chips must stay in Hong Kong, which can't power them (tomshardware.com) input gnews:38ac6220787b05226cf31f1f\n  - e2164 [party_statement; 2026-08-19; push toward_last] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang told investors that NVIDIA's China market share had fallen from 95% to zero amid the NDRC's case-by-case approval requirement for H200 purchases. | source: First Nvidia H200 shipments reach China, ByteDance and Tencent take deliveries as Beijing loosens its import block — most licensed chips must stay in Hong Kong, which can't power them (tomshardware.com) input gnews:38ac6220787b05226cf31f1f\n  - e2190 [third_party_view; 2026-08-20; push toward_first] Chinese authorities reportedly signaled recently that limited purchases of H200 chips may proceed; no authorization details or purchase volume were given. | source: Nvidia Reportedly Targets Chinese Market Comeback With Specialized AI Inference Chips — NVDA Stock Slips (stocktwits.com) input gnews:6b16161bf26adc1752bf78ff\n  - e2199 [rumour; 2026-08-20; push toward_first] ByteDance and Tencent reportedly each received roughly 10,000 Nvidia H200 processors in recent weeks; other Chinese tech firms were slated for similar allocations. | source: ByteDance, Tencent Receive 20,000 Nvidia H200 Shipments Under Relaxed Beijing Rules (techrepublic.com) input gnews:1604cc6d54ccbaf7432b13d1\n  - e2200 [third_party_view; 2026-08-20; push toward_last] China’s NDRC continues to review server orders case by case, supervising foreign-chip entry into China. | source: ByteDance, Tencent Receive 20,000 Nvidia H200 Shipments Under Relaxed Beijing Rules (techrepublic.com) input gnews:1604cc6d54ccbaf7432b13d1\n  - e2202 [rumour; 2026-08-20; push toward_last] Beijing instructed companies to keep most of their U.S.-licensed chip allotments in Hong Kong to protect and promote domestic chipmakers. | source: ByteDance, Tencent Receive 20,000 Nvidia H200 Shipments Under Relaxed Beijing Rules (techrepublic.com) input gnews:1604cc6d54ccbaf7432b13d1\n  - e2256 [third_party_view; 2026-08-21; push toward_first] Victoria Scholar said NVIDIA had started shipping H200 AI chips to China, with China sales expected to be quite small and not included in guidance for the quarter. | source: Must read weekly preview: Prudential, Nvidia (ii.co.uk) input gnews:93e9c78870df34aee36685cf\n  - e2278 [fact; 2026-08-23; push toward_first] Chinese authorities recently allowed limited imports of NVIDIA H200 chips; NVIDIA excluded Chinese data-center compute revenue from its quarterly guidance. | source: NVDA: Nvidia Earnings Put $5.2T Valuation in Waiting Mode. What Traders Need to See (tradingview.com) input gnews:d75a46ae6770d53268ac0fcb\n  - e2349 [party_statement; 2026-08-24; push toward_last] NVIDIA's forward guidance assumed zero Data Center compute revenue from China. | source: NVIDIA Earnings Preview: Can Blackwell Justify a $5 Trillion Valuation? (tastylive.com) input gnews:d6f3abdac8b80c3c4256fc18\n  - e2561 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_first] NVIDIA said Hopper 200 shipments to China-based customers were less than 1% of Q2 FY2027 Data Center revenue and were made under U.S. government licenses. | source: NVDA Q2 FY2027 Earnings Call (NVIDIA Corporation) input truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26\n  - e2562 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_last] NVIDIA's forward outlook included no China Data Center compute revenue. | source: NVDA Q2 FY2027 Earnings Call (NVIDIA Corporation) input truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26\n  - e2596 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_last] NVIDIA guided Q3 FY2027 total revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, assuming no Data Center compute revenue from China. | source: NVDA 8-K EX-99.1 (NVIDIA Corporation) input edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000073:q2fy27pr.htm\n  - e2624 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_last] NVIDIA said U.S. licenses allowed small H200 shipments to specific China-based customers, but PRC government restrictions prevented sales of all licensed products. | source: NVDA 10-Q 10-Q (NVIDIA Corporation) input edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000075:nvda-20260726.htm\n  - e2626 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_last] After the H200 charge, NVIDIA said it had shipped only a fraction of the volume allowed under U.S. licenses, with those shipments contributing less than 1% of latest-quarter Data Center revenue. | source: NVDA 10-Q 10-Q (NVIDIA Corporation) input edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000075:nvda-20260726.htm\n  - e3240 [party_statement; 2026-08-28; push toward_last] NVIDIA's Q3 FY2027 guidance assumes no Data Center compute revenue from China. | source: 🤖 NVIDIA: Can’t Build Fast Enough (appeconomyinsights.com) input gnews:86bbde98330831dcfcbd4b8f\n  - e3275 [party_statement; 2026-08-28; push toward_last] NVIDIA guided to about $108 billion of revenue for Q3, assuming no data-center compute revenue from China. | source: Video: What to Know About Nvidia’s Earnings and Meta’s $17 Billion Settlement (pro.thestreet.com) input gnews:d4e46b2cc7b58c128662060e\n  - e4375 [party_statement; 2026-09-10; push toward_last] NVIDIA's FY2027 Q3 guidance assumed zero Data Center chip sales to customers in China. | source: Nvidia's CEO Called the Dip Months Ago. Here Is How the Trade Played Out. (fool.com) input gnews:538413ed90051feff7be018e\n  - e4875 [third_party_view; 2026-09-17; push toward_first] Tom's Hardware reported that Chinese authorities often overlook gray- and black-market imports of U.S. AI chips and that official exceptions were issued to ByteDance, Alibaba, and Tencent in 2026. | source: Investigative report details how export-restricted Nvidia AI chips reach China — public records reveal how Chinese entities skirt US sanctions (tomshardware.com) input gnews:75cbbaecc2d997d4fa762033\n  - e5070 [fact; 2026-09-20; push toward_last] China's regulators mostly blocked imports of NVIDIA H200 chips; the item gives no date or amount. | source: Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang emerges as Trump's top ally in AI safety debate (cnbc.com) input gnews:11bfa6cc662ef4fee00c211a\n- A random sample of uncited evidence in force (seed 20261120):\n  - e4950 [third_party_view; 2026-09-18] C4ADS reported that roughly $13.4 million worth of restricted NVIDIA hardware moved through Southeast Asian trade routes in 50 shipments; the period is not specified. | source: $4.6 billion NVIDIA importer linked to supply network funneling restricted NVIDIA AI chips into China (tweaktown.com) input gnews:5a756c9c9da139fe7a42a2cb\n  - e4951 [third_party_view; 2026-09-18] C4ADS researchers reported missing cost, insurance, weight, and freight information, and unusually rounded customs declarations, in some shipments of restricted NVIDIA chips. | source: $4.6 billion NVIDIA importer linked to supply network funneling restricted NVIDIA AI chips into China (tweaktown.com) input gnews:5a756c9c9da139fe7a42a2cb\n  - e2197 [rumour; 2026-08-20] NVIDIA is reportedly scaling shipments of cleared H200 processors; packaging partner Amkor finished more than 1 million units in Q2 2026. | source: Nvidia plans China AI return with new specialized chip, report says (ca.finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:c258a90ec294e1838a69819d\n  - e4873 [third_party_view; 2026-09-17] C4ADS reported that Megaspeed International accounted for $4.6 billion of Nvidia hardware imports to China via shell-company structures and was the largest Southeast Asian importer of Nvidia hardware from 2023 to 2025. | source: Investigative report details how export-restricted Nvidia AI chips reach China — public records reveal how Chinese entities skirt US sanctions (tomshardware.com) input gnews:75cbbaecc2d997d4fa762033\n  - e4597 [fact; 2026-09-13] NVIDIA disclosed a first-half charge of about $400 million related to H200 products amid China sales restrictions. | source: Nvidia (NVDA) Looks Cheap on Piper’s Forecasts, but the Earnings Assumptions Are the Real Test (finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:0f0cade2e200de978df73b13\n\n  - e2851 [fact; 2026-08-26; push toward_first] NVIDIA reported $279 billion in commitments to secure supply and manufacturing capacity, up from $119 billion last quarter, including $92 billion in projected spending for the rest of the fiscal year and $87 billion in FY2028. | source: Amazon just tripled its order of Nvidia chips over ‘surging demand’ (techcrunch.com) input gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a\n  - e3636 [party_statement; 2026-09-01; push toward_first] NVIDIA’s forecast listed $92 billion in supply and capacity commitments for the remainder of FY2027. | source: Nvidia Just Gave a $267 Billion Warning That Micron Stock Could Crash Before 2029 Is Over (fool.com) input gnews:256eeb8951f1a92e56ea59ab\n  - e3637 [party_statement; 2026-09-01; push none] NVIDIA’s forecast listed $87 billion in supply and capacity commitments for FY2028. | source: Nvidia Just Gave a $267 Billion Warning That Micron Stock Could Crash Before 2029 Is Over (fool.com) input gnews:256eeb8951f1a92e56ea59ab\n  - e3638 [party_statement; 2026-09-01; push none] NVIDIA’s forecast listed $88 billion in supply and capacity commitments for FY2029. | source: Nvidia Just Gave a $267 Billion Warning That Micron Stock Could Crash Before 2029 Is Over (fool.com) input gnews:256eeb8951f1a92e56ea59ab\n  - e3639 [party_statement; 2026-09-01; push toward_first] NVIDIA’s forecast listed $6 billion in supply and capacity commitments for FY2030. | source: Nvidia Just Gave a $267 Billion Warning That Micron Stock Could Crash Before 2029 Is Over (fool.com) input gnews:256eeb8951f1a92e56ea59ab\n  - e3640 [party_statement; 2026-09-01; push toward_first] NVIDIA’s forecast listed $5 billion in supply and capacity commitments for FY2031. | source: Nvidia Just Gave a $267 Billion Warning That Micron Stock Could Crash Before 2029 Is Over (fool.com) input gnews:256eeb8951f1a92e56ea59ab\n  - e3641 [party_statement; 2026-09-01; push toward_first] NVIDIA’s forecast listed $1 billion in supply and capacity commitments for FY2032 and later. | source: Nvidia Just Gave a $267 Billion Warning That Micron Stock Could Crash Before 2029 Is Over (fool.com) input gnews:256eeb8951f1a92e56ea59ab\n  - e4025 [fact; 2026-09-05; push none] NVIDIA's $279 billion of supply and capacity commitments included $92 billion scheduled for the rest of FY2027, $87 billion for FY2028, and $88 billion for FY2029. | source: Jensen Huang Just Sent a Signal That Could Matter More Than the September Effect (fool.com) input gnews:49351bd6de4706de524baf5f\n  - e2571 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_last] NVIDIA said the largest portions of its supply commitments were concentrated in the first three years and would support production of needed products. | source: NVDA Q2 FY2027 Earnings Call (NVIDIA Corporation) input truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26\n  - e2788 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_last] Colette Kress said customer forecasts indicated demand would double in 2027, while NVIDIA could grow only 70% because of insufficient component supply. | source: Nvidia Blows Away Wall Street's 2027 Forecasts. What You Need to Know. (taekim.substack.com) input gnews:2d41619b8a2902306decca58\n  - e2800 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_last] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said available supply supported 70% growth in 2027, while demand was much higher, and said the company needed help from its supply chain. | source: Nvidia Blows Away Wall Street's 2027 Forecasts. What You Need to Know. (taekim.substack.com) input gnews:2d41619b8a2902306decca58\n  - e3390 [fact; 2026-08-30; push toward_first] NVIDIA's supply and capacity agreements can be canceled, rescheduled, or adjusted before firm orders are placed. | source: I've Covered Semiconductors for 5 Years. Nvidia Is My No. 1 Pick Heading Into 2027. (fool.com) input gnews:d77b4275dcd0a713692fe3ba\n  - e4147 [party_statement; 2026-09-07; push none] NVIDIA said some supply and capacity commitment agreements can be adjusted, potentially at additional cost. | source: Jim Cramer Wants Nvidia to Buy Back $500 Billion. Can Apple’s Playbook Work? (finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:6486d8c6fd056be68b84b2a3\n  - e4596 [fact; 2026-09-13; push toward_first] NVIDIA reported $985 million of quarterly provisions for inventory and excess purchase obligations, partly offset by releases. | source: Nvidia (NVDA) Looks Cheap on Piper’s Forecasts, but the Earnings Assumptions Are the Real Test (finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:0f0cade2e200de978df73b13\n  - e4748 [third_party_view; 2026-09-15; push toward_last] The author forecast that new production would not materially ease the global memory shortage and strained supply-demand balance before at least 2028. | source: Nvidia vs. Micron: Which Is the Better Artificial Intelligence (AI) Semiconductor Stock to Own for the Next 5 Years? (fool.com) input gnews:c8e620fc3f8fa197b570bebc\n  - e4858 [party_statement; 2026-09-17; push toward_last] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang forecast that NVIDIA would sell twice as many chips in 2027 as in 2026. | source: Jensen Huang says Nvidia will sell twice as many chips next year (cnbc.com) input gnews:f94df9a4bc981f0c32ba5797\n- A random sample of uncited evidence in force (seed 20261120):\n  - e291 [third_party_view; 2026-07-13] The author says NVIDIA carries $119 billion in supply commitments tied to hyperscaler order books. | source: Meta Vs. Nvidia: Meta Has Quietly Emerged as the Strongest Mega-Cap Alternative This Summer (247wallst.com) input gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d\n  - e4069 [fact; 2026-09-06] NVIDIA's supply commitments more than doubled to $279 billion in a quarter from $119 billion, with most of the increase attributed to memory procurement. | source: Nvidia (NVDA)’s First-Ever Year-Ahead Forecast Puts It on a Path to Pass Apple and Alphabet (finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:0af492eafa8a1c2529e56b7c\n  - e3389 [fact; 2026-08-30] NVIDIA supply and capacity commitments rose from $119 billion at the end of fiscal Q1 2027 to $279 billion at the end of fiscal Q2 2027. | source: I've Covered Semiconductors for 5 Years. Nvidia Is My No. 1 Pick Heading Into 2027. (fool.com) input gnews:d77b4275dcd0a713692fe3ba\n  - e456 [party_statement; 2026-07-15] NVIDIA guided Q2 revenue to $91.0 billion and reported $119.0 billion in booked supply commitments. | source: NVDA Vs. AMD: Even if Nvidia’s Kyber Rack AI is Delayed, It is the Better Buy Over AMD (247wallst.com) input gnews:e7ea83570963898cb3dfbb37\n  - e3688 [fact; 2026-09-01] NVIDIA reported $279 billion of supply obligations and $108.5 billion of guarantee obligations for AI-cloud and data-center partners at the close of Q2 FY2027. | source: Is Nvidia’s $35 Billion Anthropic Pact the Ultimate Circular Financing Play? (finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:d2d1a1c0a0520d170a8efdcb\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
